-- title:
--   Degeneracy images of fibre-model elements lie in j-integral closure
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $N$ a nonzero natural number, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let `fm` be a fibre model of level $N$ over $A$ with residue data $(q,k,\mathrm{red})$ — that is, a pair of subrings $B^{\mathrm{fin}}, B^{\infty}$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(N))$, realised as the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$N$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, containing the constants from $A$ and $j, j_N$ respectively $j^{-1}$, with every element integral over $A[j]$ respectively $A[j^{-1}]$, together with reduction homomorphisms to the characteristic-$q$ field $k(j,j_N)$ satisfying the stated compatibilities — and let $b$ be an element of $B^{\mathrm{fin}}$. The assertion is that there is an intermediate field $K_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$, such that for every intermediate field $K \supseteq K_0$ both images of $b$ under the two degeneracy maps to level $N q$ — the inclusion `heckeAlphaBar`, and `heckeBetaBar`, given by the substitution scaling Laurent exponents by $q$ — lie, as Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, in `jIntegralClosure (N * q) A K`: they belong to the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $K$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$, and they are integral over the subring generated by the constant series with coefficients in `coeffSubring A K` together with $j$.
--
--   This is a bookkeeping step for work on the normal model of $X_0(Nq)$ over a number field: any element of the $j$-finite chart ring of a fibre model of $X_0(N)$ becomes available, under both degeneracy maps, inside the level-$Nq$ integral closure after a finite enlargement of the base field. It is used in the analysis of prolongations of place specialisations, in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_hasValue_iff_hasValue_residueFst_zero_jIntegralClosure_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_hasValue_iff_hasValue_residueFst_zero_jIntegralClosure_of_sp_eq_spPlace) and [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_hasValue_residueFst_iff_residueSnd_jIntegralClosure_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_hasValue_residueFst_iff_residueSnd_jIntegralClosure_of_sp_eq_spPlace).
